Amy stirred eggs on the stove while Will and Amber chased each other around the kitchen, their laughter filling the room as she flipped pancakes for breakfast. A gutted face rumbled through the front door, jaws snapping at the threshold of her home. She grabbed Will by the shoulders and scooped up Amber in a quick hug, sprinting down the hallway to the back bedroom’s locked door—a safe location behind a sturdy oak frame. Turning back toward the kitchen, she slipped past the living room couch, pulling out a pistol from a hidden compartment beneath its cushion, then reached for a katana that rested on the pantry shelf and slid it into her hand. One by one, she faced the zombies: first she shot a gnarled creature with the pistol, then sliced its head off with the katana; another lunged at her, but she knocked it down with a swift thrust of the blade. More undead surged forward, each attack met with quick shots and precise slashes until every zombie fell to the floor around her. After the last one crumpled, Amy ran back through the hallway into the bedroom’s safe door, opened it, and pulled Will and Amber out together, breathing a sigh of relief as they stepped onto the kitchen floor.
